<title>JAPAN: Japan trade surplus falls 30.3 pct yr/yr in Sept.</title>
<headline>Japan trade surplus falls 30.3 pct yr/yr in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's customs-cleared trade surplus in September fell 30.3 percent from a year earlier to 779.52 billion yen, the 22nd consecutive month of year-on-year declines, the Finance Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>The merchandise surplus with the United States, often a source of trade friction, declined 8.5 percent to 398.85 billion yen in September from a year earlier. The figures were not adjusted for seasonal factors.</p>
